sentences.l:
And the Sun sprang up, leaving the very beautiful mere,
into the sky of much bronze, so that for the immortals he might shine
and for mortal men upon the grain-giving plough-land;

When they had tasted the entrails, and for the god were burning the thigh-pieces,
the others put straight in to land, and the sails of the well-balanced ship
they furled, having hauled them up, and moored her, and out they stepped themselves;

sentences.t:
ἤ τι κατὰ πρῆξιν ἦ μαψιδίως ἀλάλησθε
οἷά τε ληιστῆρες ὑπεὶρ ἅλα, τοί τ’ ἀλόωνται
ψυχὰς παρθέμενοι κακὸν ἀλλοδαποῖσι φέροντες;
